7344	Hardenbergia violacea	2022-10-10 11:25:51	iNaturalist research-grade observations	Not in a reserve	-33.929347	151.126953	\N	\N	\N	This species is Hardenbergia violacea, from the family Fabaceae and genus Hardenbergia. It is in the family Fabaceae as it’s leaves are arranged alternately and its flowers which are zygomorphic. The genus is Hardenbergia as it is a climbing plant, with alternate, compound leaves that have been modified to be 1-foliate. Its flowers consist of a standard petal, 2 wings and a keel. This is the species Hardenbergia violacea. Some stems are upright while others are climbing. Leaves are long, simple and dark green - and narrow-lanceolate shaped. They are arranged alternately along the stem, and have strongly reticulate venation. The flowers produced are purple, with a yellow/green centre on its 2 standard petals.	2022	10	10	\N	\N	\N		tresty	2022-10-10T07:31:16Z	\N	HUMAN_OBSERVATION	\N	tresty	CB Council
