7408	Oxalis debilis	2024-10-17 16:13:00	iNaturalist observations	Not in a reserve	-33.9489	150.9981	\N	\N	\N	Very typical red *Oxalis*, including typical unlined perfect spiral basal trifoliate leaves, petioles with characteristic hairs, corolla fused from the bottom and 5 flower bases. Most importantly, after taking out a small amount of its leaves for tasting, it has a very typical sour taste of *Oxalis*, which suggests that it is a kind of *Oxalis*. Because its corolla is purple-red, based on experience, we judge that this is *Oxalis corymbosa*. Because the characteristics of the *Oxalidaceae* family are relatively complex, including not only *Oxalis corymbosa*, but also woody plants such as carambola, and the identification characteristics of this plant are too obvious, so we skipped the stage of using the key and directly identified this plant as *Oxalis corymbosa*. We found this *Oxalis corymbosa* by a road in the north of Panania. When we found it, it had only two flowers, and the distribution range was not large, and the settlement was isolated. Note: The clover of the Oxalis family and the clover of the Leguminosae family look different and have their own characteristics, so they can be distinguished. Although Oxalis latifolia is also similar to the plant we obtained, its compound leaves are shaped like arrows(or triangles), which is not align with the plant we found. Thus we can conclude that it is Oxalis corymbosa.	2024	10	17	\N	\N	\N		\N	\N	\N	HUMAN_OBSERVATION	\N	tianzhou	CB Council
