7565	Dietes grandiflora	2021-10-04 03:32:00	iNaturalist research-grade observations	Not in a reserve	-33.927832	151.071746	\N	\N	\N	I have depicted this flower as a part of the Iridaceae family due to the fact that it contains 2 different types of petals which is a common aspect of the Iridaceae family. The three outer petals have a yellow strip in the middle which is only present on half of the petal. Whereas, the inner petal is mostly white with aspects of yellow towards the base. There is also 3 purple, petal like structures at the center of the flower which matches the description of the genus Dietes. The flower is radially symmetrical and also contains an inferior ovary. It forms a bush like structure, where the length of the stem is quite long and clean as it ends in 1 or more fortnight lily flowers. The leaves are a long thin strip like structure with a pointed end. It is connected from the base of the plant and contains parallel veins indicating it is a monocot plant type. The dead flowers form a hard shell like structure where there petal like structures which is hollow on the inside.	2021	10	4	\N	\N	\N		laurelrf	2021-10-20T18:52:50Z	\N	HUMAN_OBSERVATION	\N	person10661	CB Council
