8899	Allocasuarina littoralis	2022-10-19 12:42:12	iNaturalist research-grade observations	Not in a reserve	-33.929662	151.127381	\N	\N	\N	This is Allocasuarina littoralis - from the genus Allocasuarina and from the family Casuarinaceae. The family Casuarinaceae has trees with slender, wire-like branchlets. The species in this family also produce cones as fruits. While no flowers are present at the time of observation, some of the plants’ inflorescences had developed into woody structures - cones. In this family, there are only two genus - Allocasuarina and Casuarina. This species does not belong in the genus Casuarina as it seems that its cones do not have a spherical/oval shape which species from the genus Casuarina have. Allocasuarina littoralis is a species with long branchlets. Its cones grow from a short stalk/peduncle. The cones are dark brown to black in colour, and its diameter is rarely longer than its length.	2022	10	19	\N	\N	\N		tresty	2022-10-19T01:54:42Z	\N	HUMAN_OBSERVATION	\N	tresty	CB Council
