9252	Ricinus communis	2021-10-24 12:41:41	iNaturalist research-grade observations	Not in a reserve	-33.917342	151.118671	\N	\N	\N	[All these qualities can be observed within the photographs.] Firstly, this plant has distinct qualities of the Euphorbiaceae family; woody shrub with alternate leaves and fruit within a schizocarpic 3 chambered ball. Unfortunately, there were no flowers at the time. Secondly, it has distinct qualities of the Genus Ricinus; encapsulated fruit with caruncles, wide peltate leaves with toothed margins and is 7-9 palmately lobed. Thirdly, it is the species Ricinus communis as it is the only species of the genus Ricinus in the world. Otherwise, the red caruncles, green fruit and absent stipules are also features of R. communis. Extra info: The product castor oil is derived from the seeds of this plant. However, these seeds also contain a toxin called ricin, therefore raw seeds should ideally not be consumed. References include Field Guide to the Native Plants by Les Robinson (2003) and PlantNET. Photographed during the day.	2021	10	24	\N	\N	\N		faene	2021-10-24T14:49:56Z	\N	HUMAN_OBSERVATION	\N	faene	CB Council
