10440	Epacris longiflora	2020-10-19 17:14:00	iNaturalist research-grade observations	Not in a reserve	-33.929723	151.126943	\N	\N	\N	This plant is part of the Epacridaceae family. This family is closely related to Ericaceae. These plants are mostly small-leaved shrubs with parallel vennation on the leaves. The genera of this plant is Epacris. This can be seen in the photos as it is a shrub with simple leaves. The species is identified as Epacris longiflora. The petals have joined together (connate) to form one long tube. The bracts surround the flower. The leaves are roughly heart shaped and the flowers are a beautiful red and white. They are in pendant rows.	2020	10	19	\N	\N	\N		Reiner Richter	2020-10-21T08:55:17Z	\N	HUMAN_OBSERVATION	\N	louhumphries	CB Council
