12089	Wahlenbergia multicaulis	2003-03-17 00:00:00	\N	Not in a reserve	-33.887288	151.054646	\N	fertile	native	Site no. 3-1. First located 28 Oct 2002, revisited 12 Nov 2002, 17 Mar 2003. On 28 Oct 2002: Mature plants, all plants 20-40 cm high with flowers and/or capsules. Flowers deep blue opening in sunshine. Capsules have distinct red lines. On 17 Mar 2003 early season growth now dead but some new regrowth from older stems evident on most plants. Flowers, buds and fruit. Mixture of larger clumps with several stems (underground rhizomes present) and smaller, single stemmed plants. Several plants of W. gracilis recorded in Mar on upper slope in more open area with exposed soil. See more notes and photo of site with specimen sheet.	2003	3	17	Low-lying area between main rail line and siding, several metres N of small stand of Melaleuca decora. Plants found in open, grassy area adjacent to dry pond. After heavy rains this area often saturated or with standing water. Clay soils. Dominated by couch with a range of taller grasses and herbs. A mixture of native and exotic plant species. Associated species: Cynodon dactylon, Dichelachne mictantha, Lachnagrostis filiformis, Centella asiatica, Juncus usitatus, Senecio quadridentatis, S. hispidulus, Cheilanthes sieberi, Epilobium billardierianum subsp. cinereum, Wahlenbergia gracilis, Goodenia paniculata, Eragrostis brownii, Alternanthera denticulata, Fimbristylis dichotoma, Briza subaristata, B. major, Pennisetum clandestinum, Senecio madagascariensis, Cyperus eragrostis, Verbena bonariensis, Conyza albida, Bidens pilosa, Cirsium vulgare, Aster subulatus, Echinochloa crus-gallii. Extent of population 2 m x 2 m.	\N	NE corner of area 3b of the Chullora lands, between the main rail line N of area 3 and smaller rail siding extending into area 3.		Botanical Information Service	\N	\N	PRESERVED_SPECIMEN	\N	James, T.A.	CB Council
